## Patch: update distrobox-gaming ansible for DriveClub readbacks_mode fix

The `ansible/roles/seed_configs/templates/CUSA00003.json.j2` template
currently writes `readbacks_mode: 0` (Disabled). The DriveClub v1.28
investigation concluded that `readbacks_mode: 2` (Precise) is the
single required change to make the game playable — it closes the
GPU→CPU auto-exposure feedback loop. See
`docs/driveclub-investigation/phase-31-readbacks-mode-fix.md` for
the full writeup.

### Apply from the distrobox-gaming repo root

```sh
cd ~/Projects/distrobox-gaming
git apply <<'PATCH'
diff --git a/ansible/roles/seed_configs/templates/CUSA00003.json.j2 b/ansible/roles/seed_configs/templates/CUSA00003.json.j2
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/ansible/roles/seed_configs/templates/CUSA00003.json.j2
+++ b/ansible/roles/seed_configs/templates/CUSA00003.json.j2
@@ -11,7 +11,11 @@
     "internal_screen_height": 1080,
     "patch_shaders": true,
     "readback_linear_images_enabled": false,
-    "readbacks_mode": 0,
+    "readbacks_mode": 2,
     "copy_gpu_buffers": false,
     "direct_memory_access_enabled": false,
     "vblank_frequency": 60
PATCH
```

Or, if you prefer a one-line edit:

```sh
sed -i 's/"readbacks_mode": 0,/"readbacks_mode": 2,/' \
    ~/Projects/distrobox-gaming/ansible/roles/seed_configs/templates/CUSA00003.json.j2
```

### After applying

Re-seed the live config in the box:

```sh
cd ~/Projects/distrobox-gaming/ansible
ansible-playbook reset-configs.yml --tags configs
```

Or skip ansible and just verify the live file — the cleanup step
above already set it to `readbacks_mode: 2` directly:

```
cat /mnt/data/distrobox/gaming/.local/share/shadPS4/custom_configs/CUSA00003.json
```

### Optional: also add an explanatory comment

Jinja2 `.j2` templates support comments that don't render in output.
Useful if you want the *why* embedded next to the setting:

```jinja2
    {# readbacks_mode: 2 (Precise) closes the GPU->CPU auto-exposure
       feedback loop. Without it the CPU exposure integrator reads
       stale zeros and DriveClub darkens to black after ~90s of a
       race. See shadPS4 fork docs/driveclub-investigation/phase-31-*.
       Known-slow / AMD-unstable upstream — keep it per-game. #}
    "readbacks_mode": 2,
```
